Good to know:Unlike the error.js file convention which is scoped to route segments, catchError can be used to wrap any part of your component tree for component-level error recovery.Props passed to the wrapper component are forwarded to the fallback function, making it easy to create reusable error UIs with different configurations.You don't need to wrap error.js default exports with catchError. The error.js file convention already renders inside a built-in error boundary provided by Next.js.
